# tabledemo: the Table widget driving Tea v2 under a real pty (S7).
#
# The demo renders a live "cur=<cursor>" header above the 24-wide table
# (Rank/City/Population columns, 10 rows, 5-high viewport), so every cursor
# state has a UNIQUE needle.  Coverage: the first paint proves the bold
# header row (Rank + City + "Population" truncated to "Populat…" INSIDE the
# width) and the bold+fg212 selected data row (ColorAnsi256 212); j walks the
# cursor down to the bottom visible row (the cursor crossing the 5-high fold
# at cursor 5 scrolls the viewport); G jumps to the last row (top =
# rows-height); k walks back up (scrolls when the cursor crosses back above
# the fold).  q quits via the TaskQuit scan (show cursor + exit 0).
#
# Escapes: \e[?25l hide cursor, \e[?25h show cursor, \r carriage return.
expect \e[?25l\e[2Kcur=0\r\n\e[2K\e[1mRank \e[0m \e[1mCity    \e[0m \e[1mPopulat
expect \e[1;38;5;212m1     Tokyo
send j
expect cur=1
send j
expect cur=2
send j
expect cur=3
send j
expect cur=4
send j
expect cur=5
send G
expect cur=9
send k
expect cur=8
send k
expect cur=7
send q
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
